1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:04,277
Welcome to Class 15: manage the research data lifecycle.

2
00:00:04,277 --> 00:00:08,554
This video introduces the core decisions and working patterns.

3
00:00:08,554 --> 00:00:15,208
Watch the complete lesson first, then use the written class page for copyable commands,

4
00:00:15,208 --> 00:00:17,584
exercises, and detailed reference material.

5
00:00:17,584 --> 00:00:24,430
After this class, you should be able to: identify the lifecycle stage of a dataset;

6
00:00:24,430 --> 00:00:31,733
explain why instrument and research data belongs to an approved project and not a user's home

7
00:00:31,733 --> 00:00:37,666
directory; distinguish authoritative data, reproducible intermediates, durable results, records, and disposable temporary files;

8
00:00:37,666 --> 00:00:44,969
assign an owner, retention basis, access model, and review date; prepare data and metadata for reuse

9
00:00:44,969 --> 00:00:52,271
or archiving; explain when Coscine may be an appropriate archive option; follow the planned RCC-project-to-Coscine flow

10
00:00:52,271 --> 00:00:59,574
without treating it as a live self-service transfer; and require verification and acceptance before removing an

11
00:00:59,574 --> 00:01:00,486
RCC copy.

12
00:01:00,486 --> 00:01:03,779
The arrows are not a one-way conveyor belt.

13
00:01:03,779 --> 00:01:07,071
Published data may be reused and analysed again.

14
00:01:07,071 --> 00:01:10,364
An archived dataset may need a controlled correction.

15
00:01:10,364 --> 00:01:16,538
A retention decision may change when consent, law, contracts, funder rules, or scientific value change.

16
00:01:16,538 --> 00:01:22,299
At every stage, record: the accountable project owner; the approved purpose and governance basis;

17
00:01:22,299 --> 00:01:28,885
where the authoritative copy lives; who may access it; the metadata and provenance needed to interpret

18
00:01:28,885 --> 00:01:35,058
it; the retention period or review date; and the event that permits archival or deletion.

19
00:01:35,058 --> 00:01:40,820
For this course, Coscine is the planned endpoint for an eligible retained archive set.

20
00:01:40,820 --> 00:01:43,701
It is not the destination for every.

21
00:01:43,701 --> 00:01:46,746
File age alone is not a classification.

22
00:01:46,746 --> 00:01:51,967
A large old raw dataset may still be the authoritative scientific record,

23
00:01:51,967 --> 00:01:55,882
while yesterday's multi-terabyte scratch directory may already be disposable.

24
00:01:55,882 --> 00:02:00,979
RCC project storage supports active, governed computation and durable project results.

25
00:02:00,979 --> 00:02:03,760
Job-local storage supports temporary high-I/O work.

26
00:02:03,760 --> 00:02:07,003
A publication repository supports a released dataset.

27
00:02:07,003 --> 00:02:12,101
An archive supports retained data that is no longer actively changing.

28
00:02:12,101 --> 00:02:19,515
### Why project data must not live in a user's home directory A home directory is

29
00:02:19,515 --> 00:02:21,832
attached to an individual account.

30
00:02:21,832 --> 00:02:27,857
It is suitable for personal configuration, small source files, and limited working material.

31
00:02:27,857 --> 00:02:34,344
It must not become the authoritative landing area for instrument output, shared research input,

32
00:02:34,344 --> 00:02:35,734
or durable results.

33
00:02:35,734 --> 00:02:43,149
From a governance and legal-compliance perspective, approved project storage: ties processing to the project's documented purpose,

34
00:02:43,149 --> 00:02:44,539
responsible owner, and.

35
00:02:44,539 --> 00:02:50,776
Select data intentionally rather than copying an entire project tree by default.

36
00:02:50,776 --> 00:02:58,051
A reviewable package should include: The manifest should record at least the relative path,

37
00:02:58,051 --> 00:03:04,807
byte size, checksum, data class, source, format, responsible owner, access class, retention basis,

38
00:03:04,807 --> 00:03:07,406
and relationship to other files.

39
00:03:07,406 --> 00:03:13,122
Use meaningful metadata that remains useful after current team members leave.

40
00:03:13,122 --> 00:03:19,878
Do not place secrets, credentials, direct identifiers, or re-identification keys in README files,

41
00:03:19,878 --> 00:03:22,997
manifests, filenames, or general metadata fields.

42
00:03:22,997 --> 00:03:29,194
Coscine is a research-data management platform that can associate project data with structured metadata.

43
00:03:29,194 --> 00:03:36,277
Its available resource types do not all retain the same thing: some can hold data and

44
00:03:36,277 --> 00:03:41,146
metadata, while others represent or retain metadata about data held elsewhere.

45
00:03:41,146 --> 00:03:47,786
Confirm the selected resource type, allocation, protection level, retention period, and institutional approval before transfer.

46
00:03:47,786 --> 00:03:54,869
Coscine is the planned final lifecycle point for an eligible completed or stable research dataset that

47
00:03:54,869 --> 00:04:00,624
needs: an accountable project and membership model; descriptive metadata for discovery and reuse;

48
00:04:00,624 --> 00:04:07,707
a stable retained package rather than active RCC computation; and an archive period supported by the

49
00:04:07,707 --> 00:04:09,035
selected Coscine resource.

50
00:04:09,035 --> 00:04:09,477
It.

51
00:04:09,477 --> 00:04:13,250
A successful command or upload is not archive acceptance.

52
00:04:13,250 --> 00:04:19,956
Before changing or removing the RCC source, record evidence that: the intended archive set was frozen;

53
00:04:19,956 --> 00:04:26,662
file count, total bytes, and checksums match; metadata is complete enough for an independent project member;

54
00:04:26,662 --> 00:04:33,368
the destination resource contains data as well as metadata when required; access has been tested by

55
00:04:33,368 --> 00:04:40,074
an authorised person; retention and archive state are recorded; the project owner and archive owner accepted

56
00:04:40,074 --> 00:04:45,104
the transfer; and the RCC retention or deletion action was separately approved.

57
00:04:45,104 --> 00:04:51,810
When any check fails, preserve the RCC copy, record the failure, and resume from a known

58
00:04:51,810 --> 00:04:52,229
state.

59
00:04:52,229 --> 00:04:53,487
Do not repeatedly.

60
00:04:53,487 --> 00:04:59,187
Set a review date even when the archive has a defined retention period.

61
00:04:59,187 --> 00:05:04,888
Review: ownership and contact continuity; access membership; consent, legal, contractual, and funder obligations;

62
00:05:04,888 --> 00:05:11,904
whether formats and documentation remain usable; whether a persistent identifier or publication link is still correct;

63
00:05:11,904 --> 00:05:18,920
whether the data remains in scope for the selected archive; and what must happen at the

64
00:05:18,920 --> 00:05:20,235
end of retention.

65
00:05:20,235 --> 00:05:23,305
Record deletion as an accountable lifecycle event.

66
00:05:23,305 --> 00:05:29,443
The record should identify what was removed, under whose authority, when, from which locations,

67
00:05:29,443 --> 00:05:32,513
and which retained or published copies remain.

68
00:05:32,513 --> 00:05:38,543
Produce a synthetic lifecycle and archive plan that identifies the data classes,

69
00:05:38,543 --> 00:05:44,573
authoritative copy, owner, governance basis, retention decision, metadata, verification evidence, destination acceptance,

70
00:05:44,573 --> 00:05:47,086
and permitted RCC cleanup action.

71
00:05:47,086 --> 00:05:54,121
The plan must trace instrument data through project storage and job-local analysis to Coscine,

72
00:05:54,121 --> 00:06:02,161
explain why home storage is excluded, and state that the RCC-to-Coscine flow is planned and requires

73
00:06:02,161 --> 00:06:03,166
service confirmation.

